    "primaryWitnesses": [
      {
        "ref": "JOS 7:1 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "But the children of Israel committed a trespass in the devoted things; for Achan, the son of Carmi, the son of Zabdi, the son of Zerah, of the tribe of Judah, took some of the devoted things. Therefore the LORD’s anger burned against the children of Israel."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 7:18 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "He brought near his household man by man, and Achan, the son of Carmi, the son of Zabdi, the son of Zerah, of the tribe of Judah, was selected."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 7:19 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "Joshua said to Achan, “My son, please give glory to the LORD, the God of Israel, and make confession to him. Tell me now what you have done! Don’t hide it from me!”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 7:20 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "Achan answered Joshua, and said, “I have truly sinned against the LORD, the God of Israel, and this is what I have done."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 7:24 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "Joshua, and all Israel with him, took Achan the son of Zerah, the silver, the robe, the wedge of gold, his sons, his daughters, his cattle, his donkeys, his sheep, his tent, and all that he had; and they brought them up to the valley of Achor."
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 22:20 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "Didn’t Achan the son of Zerah commit a trespass in the devoted thing, and wrath fell on all the congregation of Israel? That man didn’t perish alone in his iniquity.’”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 7:21 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "When I saw among the plunder a beautiful Babylonian robe, two hundred shekels of silver, and a wedge of gold weighing fifty shekels, then I coveted them and took them. Behold, they are hidden in the ground in the middle of my tent, with the silver under it.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "JOS 7:26 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "They raised over him a great heap of stones that remains to this day. The LORD turned from the fierceness of his anger. Therefore the name of that place was called “The valley of Achor” to this day."
      }
    ],
